At 8 sec showProgress .028 due huge rendering stall? Wait earlier 2.2 sec -> .008, 8.4 sec -> .028. The app's time perhaps dt clamped and frame rate 3, so progress real time? .028 of 120 sec show = 3.4 sec. Since 3 fps*0.065 = 0.195 sim sec/s. So 8 sec real => 1.5 sec. A rocket just launching. Need wait ~30s real for first explosion. Or speed up.

Alternative spawnAt: maybe immediate flag isn't handled - bug. We should fix spawnAt to explode immediately. This is useful. Implement spawnAt: set fw.position to target, remove rocket? easiest call fw.explode() immediately and then return. `spawn()` created rocket, then fw.immediate=true. Let's fix spawnAt:
```
spawnAt(options) {
 const fw=this.spawn(options);
 fw.position.copy(fw.target);
 fw.removeRocket();
 fw.explode();
 return fw;
}
```
But explode uses this.position and removeRocket again safe. This gives immediate visual for debug. Could preserve. Need ensure if called in actual app? Search.

